    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d697">

                <pb facs="0910" n="896" sameAs="frus:frus1947v06/pg896"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">656D.006/2–547: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consulate General at
                        Batavia </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">us urgent</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-02-05">February 5,
                        1947</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>32. New York representative Isbrandtsen SS Co advised Feb 5: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“Further reference Deptel Jan 28, Dept advised Feb 4 by Zimmerman,<anchor
                                n="19" xml:id="d697-f1"/> representing Neth Emb, that NEI
                            authorities will strictly enforce new import-export regulations decreed
                            Jan 29 in Batavia. Text these new regulations not yet received by Dept.
                            Understand Zimmerman has telegraphed you his interpretation effect new
                            regulations upon your proposed commercial transaction with Perseroan
                            Bank.</p>
                        <p>Dept hereby reemphasizes to you that NEI Govt is authority recognized by
                            US Govt in entire Neth Indies.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Dept further informed Isbrandtsen, New York, Feb 5: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Dept informed<anchor n="20" xml:id="d697-f2"/> Sjahrir received cable Jan
                            29 from Isbrandtsen Co, New York, that ship <hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Martin Behrman</hi> would call at Cheribon for cargo and that
                            transaction had been approved by State Dept.</p>
                        <p>Any statement that your proposed transaction has official approval is
                            misleading. You will note from Deptel Jan 28 to you that on basis
                            assurances given you and Dept by Neth Indies Govt representative <pb
                                facs="0911" n="897" xml:id="pg897"/> Wash concerning that Govt’s
                            trade regulations, Dept registered no objection your proceeding with
                            transaction at your own risk and responsibility.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Forward text new regulations air pouch.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Marshall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d697-f1" n="19" xml:id="d697-f1-content">
                <p>E. C. Zimmerman, Trade Commissioner for the Netherlands East Indies in the United
                    States.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d697-f2" n="20" xml:id="d697-f2-content">
                <p>Telegram 38, January 31, 10 p.m., from Batavia, not printed.</p>
            </note>
